I called web_search with {"query": "potential bugs in the project"} and got: {"ok": true, "provider": "tavily", "query": "potential bugs in the project", "results": [{"title": "Common Bugs in Software Development | Gavant Blog", "url": "https://www.gavant.com/library/common-bugs-in-software-development", "snippet": "Home > Technical > Common Bugs in Software Development. # Common Bugs in Software Development. All software projects have bugs, it is inherent in their nature. Our focus here is on some of the most common bugs we have encountered. Of course, what is common on one project may not be on another. Developers will tend to follow their habits and generate some of the same sort of bugs from one project to another. We will break these down by category and severity, discuss how to test for these common bugs, and highlight some prevention strategies. In terms of severity, you can categorize in whatever way makes the most sense for your project and your team. Through Target Process, we have customized Kanban boards that will flag, or visually encode the high & critical severity issues – indicating they are first to be worked on by developers, and first to be tested by QA. These types of common bugs are frequently due to either missed- or misunderstood requirements, and most often result in a blockage of testing."}, {"title": "Programming Bugs Explained: Types, Causes, and How to Fix Them | CCM", "url": "https://www.uniccm.com/coding/bugs", "snippet": "For programmers and developers, coming across an issue in code is always constant. Bugs challenge developers to learn more and boost their critical thinking abilities to identify what is wrong and fix it. In this section, you’ll learn more about this error, including its types, common causes, and how to fix them. **In a coding context, bugs are any errors, mistakes, or unusual behaviour in the program that will prevent it from functioning correctly**. It can happen at any stage of the program development, such as during the code-writing process or even once the entire program is released. A bug cannot always be considered an obstacle, because they are an important part of software development. They encourage the developers to stop for a second and double-check their entire code, as every single line can be a potential bug. This is mainly because the logic part of a program doesn't work as it is supposed to, or there are incorrect assumptions made."}, {"title": "Why Does Software Have Bugs? 7 Causes Explained", "url": "https://www.troyweb.com/blog/7-causes-of-software-bugs-every-business-leader-should-know", "snippet": "From complex software to evolving requirements, uncover the root of unexpected results. Understanding the causes of software bugs is crucial because bugs can impact your project’s timeline, budget, and the reliability of the technology you depend on. This article explains the 7 most common causes of software bugs and how they impact software projects. By the end, you’ll have a clear understanding of why software has bugs and what you can do to minimize their impact. Software development is a complex process involving many moving parts—requirements gathering, coding, testing, integration, and ongoing maintenance. * An **error** (human mistake) leads to a **fault** (problem in the code), which can result in a **defect** (failure to meet requirements), and ultimately manifests as a **bug** (unexpected behavior in the software). The 7 causes we’ll discuss below are the most common sources of software bugs, and they map to the broader categories of software errors—whether they stem from human mistakes (errors), process gaps (faults), or external changes (defects)."}, {"title": "What Should I Do If There Are Too Many Bugs In My Software Project?", "url": "https://www.forasoft.com/blog/article/what-should-i-do-if-there-are-too-many-bugs-in-my-software-project", "snippet": "The culprits? Poor testing, shaky DevOps processes, or low-quality code. Let's break it down and show you how 2025's latest tools and trends can help you"}, {"title": "How keeping track of your development bugs is killing your Project ...", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/how-keeping-track-your-development-bugs-killing-project-tiago-palhoto", "snippet": "It's becoming more frequent having organisations demanding from their development teams a detailed track record of the bugs discovered during development!"}]}
